{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Curt Menefee (born July 22, 1965) is an American sportscaster who is the host of the Fox network's NFL show "Fox NFL Sunday".","title":"Curt Menefee"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" His co-hosts are Jimmy Johnson, Terry Bradshaw, Howie Long, and Michael Strahan.","title":"Curt Menefee"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Joseph Curtis Hennig (born October 1, 1979) is an American professional wrestler and actor currently signed to WWE, where he performs on the Raw brand under the ring name Curtis Axel.","title":"Curtis Axel"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Hennig debuted in WWE in 2010, joining The Nexus under the ring name Michael McGillicutty.","title":"Curtis Axel"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He had previously wrestled at their developmental territory Florida Championship Wrestling (FCW) and was part of the second season of "NXT".","title":"Curtis Axel"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In 2011, Hennig won the WWE Tag Team Championship with David Otunga as a member of The New Nexus.","title":"Curtis Axel"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In May 2013, Hennig reignited his career under his current ring name, paying tribute to his father "Mr. Perfect" Curt Hennig and his grandfather Larry "The Axe" Hennig and won the Intercontinental Championship.","title":"Curtis Axel"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Wiley Park Singers are an Australian children’s choir, formed in the south-west of Sydney in 1995.","title":"The Wiley Park Singers"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The choir is based in Wiley Park, Sydney, and composed of children from 29 cultural backgrounds.","title":"The Wiley Park Singers"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" They have been variously trained by music educators Lynne Woods, Vanessa Witton, Michael Strahan and Jack Liston.","title":"The Wiley Park Singers"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Chuck Versus the Break-Up" is the third episode of the second season of "Chuck".","title":"Chuck Versus the Break-Up"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It originally aired on October 13, 2008.","title":"Chuck Versus the Break-Up"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Chuck Bartowski is overcome with jealousy when his nemesis Bryce Larkin (Matthew Bomer), Sarah Walker's ex-lover and partner, makes an unexpected return.","title":"Chuck Versus the Break-Up"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Chuck and Sarah's growing feelings for each other are tested when their latest mission requires Sarah and Bryce to pose as an extremely affectionate couple.","title":"Chuck Versus the Break-Up"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Meanwhile, Morgan Grimes faces his own challenge at Buy More when he must deal with a gang of bullies, the Mighty Jocks.","title":"Chuck Versus the Break-Up"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Led by Mitt (Michael Strahan), these bullies are the employees of a neighboring sporting goods store, and they love to take over Buy More's home theater room to play sports video games.","title":"Chuck Versus the Break-Up"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Pros vs. Joes was an American physical reality game show that aired on Spike from 2006 to 2010.","title":"Pros vs. Joes"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The show featured male amateur contestants (the "Joes") matching themselves against professional athletes (the "Pros"; mostly of retired male and female pro-athletes) in a series of athletic feats related to the expertise sport of the Pro they are facing.","title":"Pros vs. Joes"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" For its first three seasons, the show was hosted by Petros Papadakis.","title":"Pros vs. Joes"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In the last two seasons, it was co-hosted by Michael Strahan and Jay Glazer.","title":"Pros vs. Joes"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The first two seasons were filmed at Carson, California's Home Depot Center, which was referenced in aerial shots.","title":"Pros vs. Joes"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Repeats can currently be seen on the El Rey Network.","title":"Pros vs. Joes"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Michael Anthony Strahan ( ; born November 21, 1971) is a media personality and former American football defensive end who spent his entire 15-year career with the New York Giants of the National Football League (NFL).","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Strahan set a record for the most sacks in a season in 2001, and helped the Giants win Super Bowl XLII over the New England Patriots in his final season in 2007.","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" After retiring from the NFL, Strahan became a media personality.","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He is currently a football analyst on "Fox NFL Sunday", and has also served as co-host on the syndicated morning talk show "Live!","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" with Kelly and Michael" with co-host Kelly Ripa from 2012 to 2016, where he was a two-time Daytime Emmy Award winner.","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In 2014, he became a regular contributor on the ABC morning television show "Good Morning America", and in 2016 the network announced that Strahan would be leaving "Live!"","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" to join "GMA" on a full-time basis.","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He starred in and produced the short-lived Fox sitcom "Brothers" and appeared as host for "Pros vs. Joes" alongside fellow Fox football analyst Jay Glazer.","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" On February 1, 2014, he was elected to the Pro Football Hall of Fame.","title":"Michael Strahan"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" As of 2016, he is the host of the ABC game show "The $100,000 Pyramid".","title":"Michael Strahan"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: They are both hosts of Fox NFL Sunday.
